// n27 — a constant whose initialiser divides by zero.
//
// The expression has no value, so the constant has none either. Reported by
// looking for the divisor rather than inferred from a fold that returned
// `None`, because a fold returns `None` for a dozen reasons and "did not
// evaluate" is not a diagnosis.
//
// omniidl 4.3.4, measured 2026-08-25:
//   Divide by zero
//
// **This is one of the three shapes that share `const-value-range` with the
// out-of-range integer of n20, and the hint is written for that one.** What a
// generator is handed here is *"widen the type — `short` to `long` … or write a
// value inside the range the message names"*, and there is no range in the
// message and no type that would hold this. The corpus had no file for the
// shape, so the false hint had never been printed. Splitting the rule is the
// fix and it lands in `orbweaver-forge`, with the hint; this file is what makes
// it measurable either way.
//
// 값이 아예 없는 경우이며, 범위를 벗어난 값과 같은 규칙에 접수된다. 그래서
// n20을 보고 쓰인 힌트가 그대로 붙는다.
module n27 {
  const long RATE = 10 / 0;
};
